- role: assistant
  content: |
    Good catch. They don’t need to be split unless you’re explicitly testing both the backend container and the Nginx proxy. For Iteration 0 you can simplify everything to the proxied URLs:

    ```
    curl http://localhost:8080/health        # root health
    curl http://localhost:8080/api/health    # API health via proxy
    curl http://localhost:8080/api/version   # version
    ```

    Those hit the backend through Nginx, which is how users will reach the service. Only fall back to port 8800 if you’re bypassing the proxy for debugging.
