- role: assistant
  content: |
    That HTML response is expected. The web container serves the React bundle at `/`, so hitting `http://localhost:8080/health` is handled by Nginx’s “frontend” rule and returns the SPA entry page.

    To check the backend health:

    - Directly hit the backend container:
      `curl http://localhost:8800/health` → JSON `{"status":"ok","env":"...","version":"..."}`

    - Or use the proxied endpoint:
      `curl http://localhost:8080/api/health` → same JSON payload.

    Likewise `http://localhost:8080/api/version` gives `{"version":"..."}`. Only paths under `/api` (and `/ws`) are proxied to FastAPI; everything else serves the frontend index.
